    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0521" n="473" sameAs="frus:frus1868p1/pg473"/>

                <head>Mr. Clay to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 213.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States, St.
                                Petersburg,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-10-19"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 19, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have just received the following note,
                    No. 6929, from the adjunct minister of foreign affairs, which I translate from
                    the French:</p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">St. Petersburg</hi>, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">October</hi> 7–19, 1868.</p>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Envoy:</hi> I have the honor to inform you that
                    the imperial ministry has duly received the two volumes containing the
                    diplomatic correspondence in reference to the late President Lincoln, which
                    accompanied the note of the United States legation of the 3–15th September last,
                    and to beg you at the same time to be pleased to transmit to the Congress the
                    thanks of the imperial government and of the chancellor of the empire for the
                    gift (l’envoi) of that publication of such great and legitimate interest.</p>
                <p>Receive, Mr. Envoy, <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c</hi>., <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >&amp;c</hi>.,</p>
                <p rendition="#right">WESTMANN.</p>
                <p>Mr. General <hi rendition="#small-caps">Clay</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >&amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. M. CLAY.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
